# Supabase security

- Browser client (`client.ts`): auth UI only, not general DB access.
- Server client (`server.ts`): session-scoped reads/writes in Server Actions and routes.
- Admin client (`admin.ts`): webhooks/cron only; imports `server-only`.
- Never import `admin.ts` from `"use client"` files.
- Every table needs RLS; default deny, then explicit policies.
- Migrations live in `supabase/migrations/` — not dashboard-only changes.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const supabase = createAdminClient();
export async function GET() {
  return supabase.from("profiles").select("*"); // admin in user path
}

// ✅ GOOD
const supabase = await createClient(); // server session client
const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();
```
